---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Tools from our Morocco directory and what each says about the DGI mandate.
// None of the invoicing apps claims DGI accreditation, and the DGI had not
// published the technical rules as of August 2026 (see the data file).
const tools = [
  { name: 'Hisab', status: 'Exports UBL 2.1 and CII, with e-signature and 10-year archiving; says it is ready for the 2026 mandate and will submit invoices to the DGI for validation; claims no DGI accreditation', fit: 'Online invoicing for SMEs and accounting firms (not a construction tool)', note: 'From 1,490 MAD a year (Starter)', href: '/ma/hisab/' },
  { name: 'Fawatir AI', status: 'Says its invoices carry ICE, IF and TVA; states it is not certified, accredited or approved by the DGI and does not transmit invoices to the tax administration', fit: 'Shops, auto-entrepreneurs, freelancers and small firms', note: 'Pro 1,699 DH a year', href: '/ma/fawatir-ai/' },
  { name: 'Aube', status: 'Says its PDFs carry the article 145 CGI mentions, with unbroken numbering and TVA by line, and that it is ready for the 2026 roadmap; claims no DGI accreditation', fit: 'SME quotes, invoices and situations (progress billing)', note: '450 DH a month excl. VAT, 2 users', href: '/ma/aube-ma/' },
  { name: 'Gestion BTP', status: 'Construction and accounting web app; DGI and CNSS exports per the vendor; e-invoicing features not confirmed', fit: 'BTP management with accounting, per the vendor', note: 'Published prices from 950 MAD HT a month, billed annually; no free trial', href: '/ma/gestion-btp-ma/' },
  { name: 'Sage Batigest Connect', status: 'Moroccan TVA, CNSS and e-invoicing features not described on the reseller page read', fit: 'Quotes, métré, invoicing and worksite tracking; accounting via Sage 100', note: 'Quote-based; no public prices in Morocco', href: '/ma/sage-batigest-connect-maroc/' },
  { name: 'Odoo', status: 'Ships a Morocco accounting localization (chart of accounts, tax report); an e-invoicing connection is not covered in our entry', fit: 'One system for quotes, projects, purchasing, invoicing and accounting', note: 'Published on odoo.com (USD); implementation extra', href: '/ma/odoo-btp-maroc/' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'When does e-invoicing become mandatory in Morocco?', a: `Hespress reported in August 2026 that e-invoicing will start in phases from the end of 2026, beginning with large companies and suppliers to the public sector. Le360, citing Challenge (June 2026), reported that SMEs follow in 2027-2028 and small firms after 2028. No firm calendar date is legally fixed yet, and the DGI had not published the technical rules as of August 2026. A pilot with volunteer companies has been running since October 2025. Treat any source quoting a specific go-live day as unverified.` },
  { q: 'What is the "clearance" model, and is it confirmed?', a: `Commentary on the Moroccan project describes a clearance (validation préalable) model: each invoice would transit a DGI platform and be validated before it is sent to the client. Hisab, for example, says it will submit invoices to the DGI for validation. But as of August 2026 the DGI had not published the final technical rules, so treat the model as announced, not final. Clearance models, used in Mexico, Turkey, Italy and Saudi Arabia, are stricter than sending a PDF, because the tax authority sees each invoice in real time.` },
  { q: 'What is the legal basis?', a: 'The obligation sits in Article 145-IX of the Code Général des Impôts (CGI). The legal foundation was first introduced by the 2018 Finance Law, and the 2024 Finance Law gave it concrete operational impetus by activating the obligation on a progressive, revenue-based schedule. Some commentary loosely calls it "the 2024 Finance Law": that is a shorthand; both Finance Laws matter.' },
  { q: 'What format will invoices use?', a: `The DGI had not published the technical rules, including the format, as of August 2026, and Fawatir AI notes that the official format for SMEs and the self-employed is not yet published. Commentary has cited structured XML (UBL 2.1 or CII) exchanged through a DGI portal, and some tools already export those formats (Hisab exports UBL 2.1 and CII), but treat the format as pending. Invoices already carry mandatory mentions: Aube lists the ICE, IF, RC, TVA detail and HT/TVA/TTC totals under article 145 of the CGI.` },
  { q: 'Who is affected, and am I (a small contractor) in scope yet?', a: `Hespress (August 2026) reports that the first phase, from the end of 2026, covers large companies and suppliers to the public sector. Le360, citing Challenge (June 2026), put the first wave at about 1,655 companies with turnover above 200 million dirhams, with SMEs in 2027-2028 and small firms after 2028; confirm these thresholds when the implementing text is published. Scope covers companies subject to corporate tax (IS) and certain taxpayers under the Bénéfice Net Réel (BNR) regime. So a small contractor is generally not in the first wave, but one that supplies the public sector should check whether the first phase applies to it, and every firm should get ready, because the direction is set.` },
  { q: 'What should I do now?', a: `Two practical steps. First, make sure your ICE appears correctly on every invoice and devis: it has been mandatory on official documents since July 2016, and Hespress reported in July 2025 that the tax administration accepts only invoices that carry it. Second, ask your invoicing software one question: "Which mandatory mentions do your invoices carry, and how will you connect to the DGI e-invoicing platform once the DGI publishes the technical rules?" If you are still on Word or Excel, choose invoicing software that stores your ICE and your clients’ ICE numbers.` },
];

const pageTitle = 'DGI E-Invoicing (Facturation Électronique) in Morocco: 2026 Guide for Contractors';
const pageDescription = `Morocco’s mandatory e-invoicing explained for the building trades: the legal basis (Article 145-IX du CGI), the announced clearance model, the phased rollout reported from late 2026 for large companies and public-sector suppliers first (with no invented go-live date), the ICE requirement, and what invoicing tools say about it. Independent; published June 2026, updated September 2026.`;

const guideUrl = new URL('/ma/guides/facturation-electronique-maroc/', Astro.site).toString();
const frUrl = new URL('/ma/fr/guides/facturation-electronique-maroc/', Astro.site).toString();
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Morocco', url: '/ma/' },
  { name: 'DGI e-invoicing for contractors', url: '/ma/guides/facturation-electronique-maroc/' },
];

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: pageTitle, description: pageDescription,
  datePublished: '2026-06-20', dateModified: '2026-09-30', inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'WrenchStack Research', url: 'https://wrenchstack.com/research/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'WrenchStack', url: 'https://wrenchstack.com' },
  mainEntityOfPage: guideUrl,
};
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} alternateUrls={[{ hreflang: 'en', href: guideUrl }, { hreflang: 'fr', href: frUrl }, { hreflang: 'x-default', href: guideUrl }]}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-orange-600">🇲🇦 Morocco · Compliance guide</p>
        <a href="/ma/fr/guides/facturation-electronique-maroc/" class="rounded-md border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-50">Français</a>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        DGI E-Invoicing (Facturation Électronique) in Morocco
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        What Morocco's mandatory e-invoicing means for the building trades: the legal basis, the announced clearance model, who is affected first, and what the tools in our directory say about it. We frame this on what has been reported, not on a deadline or format the DGI hasn't published.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">By WrenchStack Research · Published June 2026 · Timeline and tool details updated 30 September 2026 · Not tax advice: confirm your situation with the DGI (tax.gov.ma) or your fiduciaire/comptable.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-8 rounded-lg border-2 border-orange-300 bg-orange-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">⏰ The short version</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
        Morocco is introducing <strong>mandatory e-invoicing</strong>. Commentary describes a <strong>clearance model</strong>, in which each invoice is validated by a DGI platform <em>before</em> it reaches the client, but the DGI had not published the final technical rules as of August 2026. The legal basis is <strong>Article 145-IX of the CGI</strong> (introduced by the 2018 Finance Law, operationalised by the 2024 one). Hespress reported in August 2026 that it will start <strong>in phases from the end of 2026, with large companies and suppliers to the public sector first</strong>; Le360, citing Challenge, reported SMEs following in 2027-2028 and small firms after 2028. <strong>No firm go-live date is legally fixed yet</strong>, so be sceptical of any source quoting a specific day.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Late 2026</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">phased start reported, large companies and public-sector suppliers first</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Clearance</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">announced model: DGI validation before sending; final rules pending</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">ICE</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">required on invoices; mandatory on official documents since July 2016</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 prose prose-slate max-w-none">
      <h2>What is confirmed, and what isn't</h2>
      <p>It's worth being precise here, because a lot of Moroccan vendor content quotes a confident deadline the law hasn't set.</p>
      <p><strong>Confirmed:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>The DGI Director General has publicly confirmed the launch <strong>during 2026</strong>, beginning with <strong>large companies in B2B</strong>.</li>
        <li>A <strong>pilot / phase de test has run since October 2025</strong> with volunteer companies (after a public consultation that opened in October 2024).</li>
        <li>A <strong>platform-development public tender was issued in May 2024, budgeted at 6.48M MAD</strong> with a one-year delivery: the closest thing to a hard, document-backed milestone.</li>
        <li>Hespress reported in August 2026 that e-invoicing will be deployed <strong>in phases from the end of 2026</strong>, beginning with <strong>large companies and suppliers to the public sector</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Pending (do not treat as fact):</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No firm calendar go-live date.</strong> Trackers (EDICOM, VATupdate) state the start is "pending the publication of an implementing decree currently being drafted," and that the DGI has yet to publish full technical details.</li>
        <li>The first-wave <strong>threshold</strong>: Le360, citing Challenge (June 2026), reported about 1,655 companies with turnover above 200 million dirhams; confirm it when the implementing text is published.</li>
        <li>The <strong>model and format</strong>. Commentary describes clearance (pre-validation) in UBL through a DGI portal, with a later phase open to certified private operators, but the DGI had not published the final technical rules as of August 2026.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The phased rollout</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>From the end of 2026: large companies and suppliers to the public sector</strong> (Hespress, August 2026). Companies subject to corporate tax (IS), and certain taxpayers under the Bénéfice Net Réel (BNR) regime; Le360, citing Challenge, counts about 1,655 companies with turnover above 200 million dirhams in this wave.</li>
        <li><strong>2027-2028: SMEs</strong> (Le360, citing Challenge, June 2026).</li>
        <li><strong>After 2028: small firms (TPE).</strong> A small contractor is likely not in the first wave; if you supply the public sector, check whether it applies to you. The direction is set.</li>
        <li><strong>B2C and cross-border</strong> follow in later phases.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why this matters for contractors specifically</h2>
      <p>
        Moroccan trades already work to a <strong>devis → facture</strong> norm with mandatory identifiers, so the leap to structured invoicing is smaller than it looks, but two things are trade-specific. First, <strong>check what your quoting tool covers</strong>: EBP Bâtiment and Sage Batigest Connect handle quotes and invoicing, with accounting sold as a separate product, and neither of our entries describes a DGI e-invoicing connection, so the platform path matters as much as the quoting features. Second, your <strong>ICE</strong> (Identifiant Commun de l'Entreprise) has been mandatory on official documents since July 2016, and Hespress reported in July 2025 that the tax administration accepts only invoices that carry it; get it right now.
      </p>

      <h2>The wider Moroccan tax context</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>TVA:</strong> 20% standard, with reduced rates of 14%, 10% and 7%. Your software must apply the right rate per line.</li>
        <li><strong>IS (corporate tax):</strong> progressive, mid-reform; rates shift each Finance Law.</li>
        <li><strong>SIMPL</strong> (simpl.tax.gov.ma) is the DGI's existing online portal for télédéclaration/télépaiement of TVA, IS and IR; the DGI had not published how e-invoices will be transmitted as of August 2026.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the tools in our directory say</h2>
      <p>
        From the software in our <a href="/ma/">Morocco directory</a>, here is what each tool says about the mandate, or what our entry could not confirm. <strong>None of the invoicing apps (Hisab, Fawatir AI, Aube) claims DGI accreditation</strong>, and the DGI had not published the technical rules as of August 2026. Treat "ready for 2026" as a vendor claim, and ask vendors the concrete question below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border border-slate-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-left text-slate-700">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Tool</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">E-invoicing position</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Scope</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Pricing</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 bg-white">
          {tools.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-slate-900"><a href={t.href} class="hover:text-orange-600">{t.name}</a></td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">{t.status}</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-600">{t.fit}</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-600">{t.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">The e-invoicing column reports what each vendor says, or what our entry could not confirm, as checked in September 2026. None of it is a DGI accreditation. Confirm directly with each vendor.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">The one question to ask any vendor</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        Don't assume a good quoting tool covers the mandate. Ask: <strong>"Which mandatory mentions (ICE, IF, TVA) do your invoices carry, and how will you connect to the DGI e-invoicing platform once the DGI publishes the technical rules?"</strong> If the answer is vague, that's your signal. And confirm your <a href="/ma/ice-identifiant-commun-entreprise/" class="font-medium text-orange-700 hover:underline">ICE</a> is correct on every document today.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-slate-900">{f.q}</summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-5 text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-slate-700">Sources &amp; verification:</strong> First published June 2026 from EDICOM, VATupdate, Upsilon Consulting, Experio and Sage Maroc. Updated 30 September 2026 from our re-verified directory entries: the timeline from Hespress (August 2026) and Le360 citing Challenge (June 2026), and each tool’s own statements. Legal basis: Article 145-IX du CGI (introduced by the 2018 Finance Law, operationalised by the 2024 Finance Law). Reported: phased start from the end of 2026 with large companies and public-sector suppliers first, pilot since October 2025, the 6.48M MAD platform tender (May 2024). Pending and explicitly NOT stated as fact here: the clearance model and invoice format (DGI technical rules not published as of August 2026), the exact go-live date and the first-wave threshold. General information, not tax advice. Spotted an error? <a href="/contact/" class="underline">Tell us</a>.
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900 p-8 text-white">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Compare Moroccan trades software & services</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">Independent reviews of Moroccan BTP software, tender intelligence, CNSS payroll and mandatory construction insurance, with no pay-to-play.</p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/ma/" class="rounded-md bg-orange-500 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-orange-600">🇲🇦 Morocco directory →</a>
        <a href="/ma/compare/" class="rounded-md bg-white px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-100">Compare vendors</a>
        <a href="/for-vendors/" class="rounded-md border border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-white/20">Are you a vendor? Work with us</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
